This directory is the l5-r1-probe service's ONLY build trigger.

The service's Railway watchPatterns are
deploy/l5_r1_probe/ENABLE_REDEPLOY_BY_OWNER_ONLY/** and nothing else, so an
ordinary push to the branch produces a SKIPPED deployment and the running
probe is left alone. Touching a file in here is what asks for a build.

Do not touch it to "refresh" anything. Each line below records one authorised
deploy and why the owner asked for it.

2026-09-16  OWNER P0: the complement-acceptance probe placed a money-moving
            BUY that the per-market notional counter did not see, so the
            advertised $0.05 envelope was really $0.06. Deploying the
            correction (one counter, tested before submission, partials
            reconciled) DISARMED. No arming variable is set by this deploy.

2026-09-16  HALT. The owner authorised R1 for ONE market and said "Once the
            first market reaches the campaign stop condition, HALT AND REPORT
            ... Do not automatically start R1 market #2." The held market
            (aec-itfwo-meiguo-junzha) settled REALIZED -0.0214 at 07:44:32Z and
            the campaign's own reselect loop immediately advanced to further
            markets. That is invariant 5 -- "no second market is selected" --
            contradicted, and the owner's rule for a contradiction is HALT
            IMMEDIATELY.

            This deploy carries NO code change and NO arming variable. It
            exists only to apply a Railway startCommand that exports
            PMUS_SPRING_SHUTDOWN=1 and PMUS_SPRING_LIVE=NO before the same
            image CMD. shutdown_requested() is tested BEFORE armed(), so the
            process boots straight into safe_shutdown: cancel OUR outstanding
            orders, verify against a FRESH /v1/orders/open read, preserve held
            inventory to settlement, never place, never liquidate.

            WHY A startCommand AND NOT A VARIABLE, stated plainly because a
            startCommand is exactly what condemned the legacy probe: the
            Railway set-variables tool is not offered to this session and
            redeploy has no snapshot to copy (the latest deployment is
            SKIPPED), so this was the only path that could reach the cancel.
            It differs from the legacy one in the way that matters -- it
            rewrites NO source, runs no sed, and keeps the image's own
            SERVICE_ROLE guard. It must be REMOVED once the owner restores a
            variable path; it is a stop, not a configuration.

2026-09-16  OWNER: rebuild the live execution envelope as an immutable
            per-authorization MANDATE, and replace the emergency runtime
            override with a durable fail-closed mechanism.

            This deploy ships the image that can halt itself from a committed
            file. analysis/l5/authorization/HALT is COPYed in and read by
            shutdown_requested() before armed() is consulted, so the service
            comes back HALTED with no platform API involved. The authorization
            to spend is a second, separate file -- live_mandate.json -- and it
            is deliberately ABSENT, so even an un-halted process has no
            envelope and refuses every order at the wire.

            NO ARMING VALUE IS SET BY THIS DEPLOY. The probe comes back halted
            and unauthorized, which is the state the owner asked for.

            Once this build is verified SHUTDOWN_VERIFIED from the FILE, the
            emergency startCommand set on 2026-09-16 is removed and the service
            redeployed from the snapshot, so the running system is the reviewed
            artifact again rather than the artifact plus a runtime override.
